Omitted scenes: the surface stage. Done means: an omitted span renders greyed/struck-through (Final Draft's visual language — muted ink, not hidden), is not editable (clicking into it does not place a caret), and the Navigator marks it. Pagination: measure what Final Draft 13.4 does with the fixture first — does the omitted scene count toward page numbers? — follow it, and report what you measured. Edits outside the span stay exactly as today; the IL-0071 save behavior (file's bytes win, FDX_REWRITE_OMITTED_SCENE_KEPT) must keep passing untouched.